{"title":"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A straight one-mile stretch of highway, 40 feet wide, is closed. Robert rides his bike on a path composed of semicircles as shown. If he rides at 5 miles per hour, how many hours will it take to cover the one-mile stretch?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71a0b57907e6bd351febe1d78fad2839d5131421.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(10cm); pathpen=black; pointpen=black; D(arc((-2,0),1,300,360)); D(arc((0,0),1,0,180)); D(arc((2,0),1,180,360)); D(arc((4,0),1,0,180)); D(arc((6,0),1,180,240)); D((-1.5,-1)--(5.5,-1));[/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"138\" />\nNote: 1 mile = 5280 feet\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c91a475829e5cbdd00db1426252ec6730c30cd09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{\\pi}{11}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{\\pi}{10}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"414\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>There are two possible interpretations of the problem: that the road as a whole is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet wide, or that each lane is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet wide. Both interpretations will arrive at the same result. However, let us stick with the first interpretation for simplicity. Each lane must then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet wide, so Robert must be riding his bike in semicircles with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet and diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet. Since the road is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/c/2fc92cb8cdff39ca4dac9ec6fb3224dbe5fa50a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5280$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> feet long, over the whole mile, Robert rides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d4a5093b3e4297035b4804707810f8f6b5b16b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5280}{40} =132$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" /> semicircles in total. Were the semicircles full circles, their circumference would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86fd9eb5a5c016caaa2ede0062581473fa439184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi\\cdot 20=40\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" /> feet; as it is, the circumference of each is half that, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cf5d779e3740a6916b73852f858ab4a72c82e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\pi$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> feet. Therefore, over the stretch of highway, Robert rides a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/2/4f24b805dcc743fc6e6277172520d767a7873276.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$132\\cdot 20\\pi =2640\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"140\" height=\"13\" /> feet, which is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aeebb746f8c0d3dac5219c3635617032430afee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" /> miles. Robert rides at 5 miles per hour, so divide the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aeebb746f8c0d3dac5219c3635617032430afee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" /> miles by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mph (because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8b3cd511f74e21a0af276dcae0e3754fd0bf9a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = \\frac{d}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"39\" /> and time = distance/rate) to arrive at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42e75f2ff032ca9516cfb85369ae47ce9e9c4bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{\\pi}{10}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"68\" height=\"44\" /> hours.\n</p><p>Edit: If you are confused about the lanes, watch the video below&#160;:)\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zi01koyAVhM\">https://youtu.be/zi01koyAVhM</a> ~savannahsolver\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 8\">2014 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2014\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" titl